  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Tooling improvement; no new kappa.**\n\nThis opt-in tool speeds up the historical ternary frame checker by caching results for exact ordered frame pairs. It retains both orientations, every physical edge, and the existing rational arithmetic. Complete matrix-and-edge transcripts and published small-control fields for h=8 and h=9 match the retained checker. Timings use alternating fresh processes. The h=29 construction is not replayed, and kappa is unchanged.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- Base: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`. Seed: **93**.\n- Scope: `ternary-h8-h9-physical-edge-pair-memoization`; [task card](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/cb5a79f12531022c6fcd2fe592b5030d4e3ae9e7/research/ternary-frame-cache/CLAIM.json), [20 exact source pins](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/cb5a79f12531022c6fcd2fe592b5030d4e3ae9e7/research/ternary-frame-cache/SOURCES.json).\n- Nearest work: #154 (scheduling/paired-cube frames), #367 (PR364 integer elimination). Object here: historical `ternary_side.verify_invocation_frames`; original rational routines and full schedule retained.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/ternary-frame-cache/verify.py --out /tmp/ternary-frame-cache-93 --pairs 3\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_IDENTICAL_TERNARY_FRAME_REPLAY 84672 edges; ... ratio of medians`. Fresh output directory required.\n\n| Local Python 3.14.6 / macOS arm64, three alternating pairs | Reference | Cached |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Median wall seconds | 11.525 | 6.775 |\n\nRatio of medians: **1.70**. Peak RSS: **96.30 \u2192 105.17 MiB**. Shared host; OS caches not flushed.\n\n- Exact comparison: all **84,672** ordered edge records, full rational matrices, graph and scalar receipts.\n- **18 tests** on Python 3.11 and 3.14; full replay on both; **5 original ternary tests**; selected-source binding passed.\n- Controls: singular Gram, missing common pair, non-idempotence, wrong target/role, rank-only and hash-collision keys, reversed transitions, all 20 source mutations, transcript omissions/duplicates/reordering, disabled assertions, reused output.\n- Excluded: h=29 DAG/full historical assembly, selected cold replay, all-size multiplication proof.\n- Retained source, `upstream/`, selected certificate and default checker: unchanged.\n\n[Adapter diff](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/cb5a79f12531022c6fcd2fe592b5030d4e3ae9e7/research/ternary-frame-cache/evidence/ADAPTATION.diff) \u00b7 [Timing and exact receipts](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/cb5a79f12531022c6fcd2fe592b5030d4e3ae9e7/research/ternary-frame-cache/evidence/benchmark-python314.json) \u00b7 [Validation](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/cb5a79f12531022c6fcd2fe592b5030d4e3ae9e7/research/ternary-frame-cache/evidence/validation.json)\n\n## Credit\n\nDouglas Colkitt wrote the retained checker. Zhihao Chen's [PR7](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/7) supplied the earlier five-subset motif and common-pair geometry. Hanson Sun prepared this contribution with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. See CLAIM.json for scope, SOURCES.json for pins, and evidence/ for checks and measurements. Apache-2.0.\n",
